---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Supergut POS — point of sale for iPad"
  description="A free iPad point of sale for retail shops, with cash, configured Teya payments and connected business systems. Product information, setup, support and privacy."
>
  <article class="product-page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Supergut POS · iPad</span>
      <h1>Point of sale for your shop.</h1>
      <p>
        Browse or scan merchandise, build a basket, choose a customer and record
        cash or configured card payments. Keep unpaid work, find completed
        transactions and prepare customer receipts using native printing and
        email workflows.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Product information">
        <a href="/pos/support/en/">Support and setup</a>
        <a href="/pos/privacy/en/">Privacy notice</a>
        <a href="/pos/" lang="is" hreflang="is">
          Íslenska
        </a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/pos/ipad-demo.png"
        width="1312"
        height="1902"
        alt="Supergut POS sample shop on an iPad simulator, showing product cards, search and basket controls."
      />
      <figcaption>
        Development preview with sample data and simulated payments.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Availability and requirements</h2>
      <p>
        The first App Store release is being prepared. A public download link is
        not available yet. Supergut POS targets iPad with iPadOS 18 or later,
        with Icelandic and English interfaces. The app is free; payment
        processing, hosting and connected third-party services may require
        separate agreements and fees.
      </p>
      <p>
        A connected merchant needs a configured Supergut POS backend, an iPad
        pairing code from its administrator and cashier access. Configured Teya
        card payments require a supported terminal, merchant agreement and
        enabled payment method. Receipt output requires the selected printer or
        an email account on the iPad.
      </p>
      <h2>Try the sample shop</h2>
      <p>
        In an installed build, choose <strong>Try demo</strong> to explore the
        interface without an account, server or terminal. Sample payments are
        simulated and sample sales are not posted to Business Central. This does
        not enable offline processing of real card payments.
      </p>
      <h2>Connected business systems</h2>
      <p>
        Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central and optional Netgíró, gift-card
        and customer-credit workflows depend on the merchant's configuration. A
        completed till sale and completed accounting posting are separate
        outcomes. Each enabled integration needs acceptance in the merchant's
        environment before real trading. Teya instalment payments are outside
        the first-release scope.
      </p>
      <h2>Help and privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Supergut POS is provided by Supergut ehf, Icelandic registration number
        430524-2160. For setup, receipts, payment recovery or a data request,
        use <a href="/pos/support/en/">Supergut POS support</a>. Read{" "}
        <a href="/pos/privacy/en/">how your information is handled</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .product-page {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }
  .page-heading nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  figure {
    margin: 0 0 40px;
  }
  img {
    display: block;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 480px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    border-radius: 20px;
  }
  figcaption {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
